.TH DELEGATED 8 "" "DeleGate 9.9.13" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
delegated \- DeleGate multi-protocol proxy server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B delegated
.RB [ \-P\fIport\fR ]
.RB [ \-f ]
.RB [ \-r ]
.RB [ \-F\fIfunc\fR ]
.RB [ \-v[vdtsau] ]
.RB [ +=\fIconfigfile\fR ]
.RI [ name = value ]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B delegated
relays HTTP, FTP, SMTP, NNTP, POP, Telnet, SOCKS and other protocols.
It runs as a forward proxy, a reverse proxy, a gateway between protocols or a TLS terminator.
Behaviour is set by parameters of the form
.IR name = value
on the command line, in the environment or in a file loaded with
.BR += .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-P port
Entrance port or ports, for example
.BR \-P8080 .
Required unless a
.B \-F
function is used.
.TP
.B \-f
Stay in the foreground and keep the current directory.
.TP
.B \-r
Stop a DeleGate that runs on the same port before starting.
.TP
.BI \-F func
Run a built-in function and exit, for example
.B \-Fver
(version and libraries),
.B \-Fparam
(parameter help) or
.B \-Fkill
(stop the server of a port).
.TP
.B \-v
Run in the foreground and write the log to the terminal.
.TP
.BI += file
Load parameters and options from
.IR file .
.TP
.IB name = value
Set a parameter.
.B DGROOT
must be given on the command line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/delegate/delegated.conf
Configuration loaded with
.BR += .
The package installs
.I delegated.conf.example
next to it.
.TP
.I /etc/delegate/certs
Certificates and keys for TLS (CERTDIR).
A self-signed certificate is generated here when none exists.
.TP
.I /var/lib/delegate
DGROOT with administration files, work and temporary files.
.TP
.I /var/log/delegate
Log files (LOGDIR).
.TP
.I /var/cache/delegate
Cache files (CACHEDIR).
.TP
.I /run/delegate
Files of active servers (ACTDIR).
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/delegate/doc/reference/parameters.md
Parameter reference.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/delegate/doc/README.md
Index of the documentation.
.SH SYSTEMD
The unit
.B delegated.service
starts
.B delegated
as user
.B delegate
in the foreground:
.PP
.RS
.nf
systemd-sysusers
systemd-tmpfiles \-\-create
cp /etc/delegate/delegated.conf.example /etc/delegate/delegated.conf
systemctl enable \-\-now delegated
.fi
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
HTTP proxy on port 8080:
.PP
.RS
.nf
delegated \-P8080 SERVER=http ADMIN=root@example.com
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reverse proxy for an origin server:
.PP
.RS
.nf
delegated \-P8080 SERVER=http "MOUNT=/* http://origin.example.com/*"
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.I /usr/share/doc/delegate/doc/README.md
(documentation),
.BR systemd.service (5),
.BR sysusers.d (5),
.BR tmpfiles.d (5)
